Quick start
===========

A minimal bilirubin run on two workers. Three files carry the worker count and must agree; bbb is
a source constant, so it is set before compiling.

  ./fix_paths.sh                          # set the conda environment and MOPAC-PI path

  cd reaction_discovery_2025/bilirubin_pm6fom_FINAL

  sed -i 's/^bbb=400/bbb=2/'     p.f90              # worker count, line 35
  sed -i 's/^xt=400/xt=2/'       loadFoundlings.sh  # line 21
  sed -i 's/{1\.\.399}/{1..2}/'  batch30.sh         # line 3

  module load intel-oneapi
  ifort p.f90 -o a.out
  ( cd oldSecondary      && ifort s2.f90 -o b.out )
  ( cd oldSecondary/test && ifort s3.f90 -o c.out && ifort convert.f90 -o convert.out )

  ./regenerate_workers.sh 2               # clone oldSecondary into secondary1 and secondary2
  sbatch saout.sh                         # driver: creates the buckets, seeds yesfolder, runs a.out
  ./batch30.sh                            # submit the workers

Progress:

  cat measur.txt                          # current point, shell counter, flags
  ls allfolder | wc -l                    # points evaluated in the current shell
  tail -3 slurm-out                       # driver log: shell completion and the next ceiling

Stop:

  scancel --name=pm6fomo
  scancel --name=pm7s

DASA, aqueous
-------------

  cd reaction_discovery_2025/dasa_yowy_re5

  sed -i 's/^bbb=399/bbb=2/'     p.f90              # line 36
  sed -i 's/^xt=399/xt=2/'       loadFoundlings.sh  # line 4
  sed -i 's/{1\.\.399}/{1..2}/'  batch30.sh         # line 3

  module load intel-oneapi
  ifort p.f90 -o a.out
  ( cd oldSecondary && ifort 1s.f90 -o a.out && ifort s2.f90 -o b.out )

  ./loadFoundlings.sh
  sbatch saout.sh
  ./batch30.sh

This campaign additionally requires ChemShell 3.7.1 with a working MPI, ORCA and xTB; the worker
submit.sh exports them. The bilirubin campaign requires none of these, as MOPAC-PI runs serially.

Notes
-----

  - gfortran rejects p.f90 unless -fallow-argument-mismatch is given, because addTo is called with
    an integer literal where the dummy argument is real(8). ifort compiles it as written.

  - The first shell runs at the seed energy itself, so no move is accepted until the ceiling opens
    at the second shell, where ecut = Ecut0 + incr. With the production EcutMax a two-worker
    demonstration therefore finishes after two shells.
